<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaifeng</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaifeng is a city in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> plain. It was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Northern Song</a> and one of the largest and most commercialised cities of its time. It fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin in 1127, ending the Northern Song period of the Song Dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaifeng.jpg" alt="Kaifeng" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: caoyuan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%BE%99%E4%BA%AD%E5%85%AC%E5%9B%AD_-_panoramio_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
